@startuml
title NestJS — ingestion simulation Kafka sem HTTP loopback (v1.3.0 proposta)
queue "Kafka simulation" as Broker
participant "RoutesDriverConsumer" as Consumer
participant "RoutesDriverService" as Service
database "Prisma MongoDB" as Prisma
participant "RoutesDriverGateway" as Gateway
Broker -> Consumer : @MessagePattern simulation (route_id,lat,lng)
Consumer -> Service : processRoute()
Service -> Service : validar ID e coordenadas
alt inválidos
 Service --> Consumer : BadRequestException
 Consumer --> Broker : erro propagado
else válidos
 Service -> Prisma : routeDriver.upsert()
 alt falha banco
  Prisma --> Service : erro
  Service --> Consumer : erro sem WebSocket
 else commit
  Prisma --> Service : registro salvo
  Service -> Gateway : emitNewPoints()
  Service --> Consumer : registro salvo
 end
end
note bottom
No Kafka real, retry e deduplicação ainda requerem contrato.
HTTP externo process-route continua presente e deve ser protegido.
end note
@enduml
